3. B6 (adversarial corpus): FAIL
--------------------------------

What is fixed: mathd/Cargo.toml has no [dependencies]; tests/corpus.rs parses
JSON by hand; the mathd CI run on a3f3396 (39990111771) shows

  Running tests/corpus.rs (target/debug/deps/corpus-a38928ccc323c767)
  test sympy_ground_truth_corpus_is_accepted_and_mutants_rejected ... ok
  test result: ok. 1 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 0.11s

must_reject (tests/corpus.rs lines 296-318) panics on Unverifiable, so an
unverifiable mutant cannot pass silently. Every correct answer carries a SymPy
call and result.

What fails is the corpus itself, against the work order (docs/work-orders.md
section B6: "spanning a Class 11-12 maths syllabus", wrong answers "of the kind
a language model actually produces - sign error after integration by parts,
dropped constant of integration, omitted chain rule, ignored domain"):

