Findings
  B6-F1 (blocking) Not a syllabus. Four templates, each swept over one integer
        parameter 125 times. No definite integrals, integration by parts,
        substitution, logarithms, inverse trigonometry, limits, matrices or
        determinants, sequences and series, differential equations, vectors or
        complex numbers.
  B6-F2 (blocking) The wrong answers are mechanical: "correct + x", "correct -
        x", "+1", "-1", a root off by one from the largest root, a factor off by
        one. None of the four error kinds the spec names appears. For
        integral_125 the error a model actually makes is exp(25*x) (omitted
        chain-rule factor 1/25) or 25*exp(25*x); neither is in the corpus.
  B6-F3 (blocking) "Ignored domain" needs claims that are true only on part of
        the real line (sqrt(x^2) = x, log(x^2) = 2*log(x)). The corpus has none,
        so the B5 V1 failure mode (wrong only for x < 0) is not exercised.
  B6-F4 (note) A derivative check cannot reject a missing "+ C"; an
        antiderivative without C is correct. Read "dropped constant" as a
        dropped multiplicative constant and say so in the generator docstring.

The verifier scoring 100% on an easy corpus is not the finding the work order
asks for. Fix the corpus, not the verifier, and do not tune either to the other.


